{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "05-archon-providers-map",
  "title": "Archon providers and the kernel",
  "description": "How Archon calls agents, and where Ford's agent kernel would plug in.\n\n- **Top:** the Archon engine's DAG executor (dag/run-layers.ts) calls `sendQuery()` on the IAgentProvider contract, which yields a Chunk stream that ends in one result chunk (carries `tokens`). The executor reads Capabilities first, before dispatch. Stickies list the chunk types, the capability flags and ExecutionContext.\n- **Middle:** the Providers. Claude Code, Codex and Pi exist today. The agent-kernel provider (violet, dashed wires) is proposed.\n- **Bottom right:** what lives outside Archon (Ford's setup): Token Gateway, which gets the model traffic from every provider, and kernel.spawnAgent, which the kernel provider would wrap.\n- **Bottom left:** one event, two shapes. The workflow_events row the executor appends, and the trace_events envelope the kernel provider would write, joined by a proposed bridge. Pink boxes are the three fields the Archon row lacks.\n\nKey: a solid wire exists today. A dashed violet wire is proposed.",
